Everything is in place. Here's a summary of what was implemented across both files:

---

### `app/auth.py` — Authentication

`require_api_key` now validates the `X-API-Key` header against `VALID_API_KEYS`. Returns 401 with `"Missing API key"` when the header is absent, `"Invalid API key"` when the key isn't in the dict. Returns the username on success.

### `app/main.py` — 5 endpoints

| Endpoint | What it does |
|---|---|
| `GET /tasks` | Added optional filters: `status` (enum), `priority` (int), `assigned_to` (str). Added `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 20) for pagination. All filters are combinable. |
| `POST /tasks` | Requires auth via `Depends(require_api_key)`. Validates `project_id` exists (404 if not). Auto-generates ID from `max existing + 1`. Returns 201 with the created task. |
| `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` | Requires auth. Partial update — only non-`None` fields in `TaskUpdate` are applied. Returns 404 if not found. |
| `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` | Requires auth. Removes the task from the in-memory list. Returns 204 on success, 404 if not found. |

All 15 smoke-test assertions passed: no-auth rejection, invalid-project rejection, valid creation with auto-ID, partial update, delete with cascade-verify, invalid-key rejection, combined filtering, and pagination slicing.
